{"run":"FLY-1410 B/A test","rounds":[{"r":0,"y":0,"total":3,"added":3},{"r":1,"y":6000,"total":12,"added":9},{"r":2,"y":12000,"total":22,"added":10},{"r":3,"y":18000,"total":30,"added":8}],"count":30,"items":[{"id":"2087524570773213330","au":"0xwhrrari","t":"2026-08-12T13:00:16.000Z","url":"https://x.com/0xwhrrari/status/2087524570773213330","text":"Andrew Ng just gave away a free 59-minute masterclass\n\nOn the AI stack most builders still overlook:\n\n01:40 - Why agent loops beat one-shot prompts\n04:00 - The orchestration layer above every model\n06:20 - Why coding by hand is fading away\n10:50 - Build 20 prototypes instead of"},{"id":"2087468069509591117","au":"gippp69","t":"2026-08-12T09:15:45.000Z","url":"https://x.com/gippp69/status/2087468069509591117","text":"ANTHROPIC ENGINEERS JUST SHOWED WHY A 4-LEVEL AGENT STACK CAN BURN 10X THE TOKENS FOR A PROBLEM THAT NEEDED 1 CALL\n\nanthropic’s rule is simple. start with the smallest system that works and only add another layer when the current one actually breaks\n\nrest call ? tool loop ?"},{"id":"2087513648243597554","au":"Av1dlive","t":"2026-08-12T12:16:52.000Z","url":"https://x.com/Av1dlive/status/2087513648243597554","text":"this is the most impressive GitHub repo I have ever seen \n\nwith 5,000 stars. this is f**king gold.\n\nsomeone figured out how to run Kimi K3 on any laptop for free.\n\n[here is how to set it up in 2 mins]\n\n1. git clone FareedKhan-dev/kimi-k3-in-c\n2. make\n3. ./bin/k3 --preset laptop"},{"id":"2087262250432376833","au":"Argona0x","t":"2026-08-11T19:37:54.000Z","url":"https://x.com/Argona0x/status/2087262250432376833","text":"somebody is getting rich off this tonight\n\non august 5 Zuckerberg launched Meta's coding agent and led with the feature: \"Muse Code distributes complex tasks to sub-agents rather than having one agent do everything.\"\n\nAnthropic spent the same fortnight shipping a line into Claude"},{"id":"2087506344911720711","au":"beamnxw","t":"2026-08-12T11:47:51.000Z","url":"https://x.com/beamnxw/status/2087506344911720711","text":"This paper is f*cking brilliant\n  \nA computer science survey mapped 150+ agent memory architectures across 90 pages to build self-evolving long-horizon agents  \n  \nThe result: a 3D taxonomy showing action-based memory and self-evolving structures boost long-horizon retention by"},{"id":"2087518688048034268","au":"Roxx_0x","t":"2026-08-12T12:36:54.000Z","url":"https://x.com/Roxx_0x/status/2087518688048034268","text":"MY CLAUDE DREAMS NOW.\n\nevery night a dream pass reads what it learned, merges the duplicates, forgets the noise. every morning it wakes up sharper than it went to sleep.\n\nthe whole setup is two markdown files - both on the board, with the exact install line. pause on either file"},{"id":"2087236464228827621","au":"techNmak","t":"2026-08-11T17:55:26.000Z","url":"https://x.com/techNmak/status/2087236464228827621","text":"Two phases run under every LLM call\n\nPrefill and decode.\n\nPhase 1: PREFILL\n- Your prompt first gets tokenized. Conceptually, \"Why is the sky blue?\" might look like [Why] [is] [the] [sky] [blue] [?].\n- Then the model processes the prompt through its transformer layers, with"},{"id":"2087209715965313367","au":"akshay_pachaar","t":"2026-08-11T16:09:09.000Z","url":"https://x.com/akshay_pachaar/status/2087209715965313367","text":"Your memory shouldn't wait for queries.\n\nEvery agent memory system today does the same two things. It stores facts and it retrieves the right ones when you ask.\n\nThat design assumes you already know what to ask for. You get back exactly what you queried, and nothing about what"},{"id":"2087510301982028028","au":"alex_verem","t":"2026-08-12T12:03:34.000Z","url":"https://x.com/alex_verem/status/2087510301982028028","text":"An engineer got so tired of decoding Claude's writing that he built a plugin that translates it into plain English. 2.3K upvotes on Reddit say he's not alone.\n\nIt's called claudish-to-english. He tried simplified-English instructions first, even the aerospace writing standard."},{"id":"2087294922378637680","au":"zackkanter","t":"2026-08-11T21:47:44.000Z","url":"https://x.com/zackkanter/status/2087294922378637680","text":"Mostly solvable. Have agents incorporate the following:\n\n- \nhttps://\ntbaggery.com/2008/04/19/a-n\note-about-git-commit-messages.html\n…\n- \nhttps://\ncbea.ms/git-commit/\n- ASD-STE100 / Simplified Technical English + Google developer documentation style guide"},{"id":"2087163414439235666","au":"josesilesdata","t":"2026-08-11T13:05:10.000Z","url":"https://x.com/josesilesdata/status/2087163414439235666","text":"BYE to paying for AWS just to practice!!\n\nYou can have the ENTIRE AWS on your laptop.\n\n- Free.\n- No credit card \n- No account\n\nIt's called Floci.\n\nYou get 69 AWS services on localhost:4566.\n\n- S3\n- EKS\n- IAM\n- Athena\n- Lambda\n- DynamoDB\n- API Gateway\n- Step Functions\n\nAnd many"},{"id":"2087555554830852538","au":"DeRonin_","t":"2026-08-12T15:03:23.000Z","url":"https://x.com/DeRonin_/status/2087555554830852538","text":"somebody built a live feed of validated startup ideas you can copy\n\nhere is the link: \nhttp://\nearly.tools\n\nhundreds of early-stage AI products, most too new to be covered anywhere\n\nevery tool on there is a founder who already tested a market and proved demand exists.. you're"},{"id":"2087293827002638525","au":"defileo","t":"2026-08-11T21:43:23.000Z","url":"https://x.com/defileo/status/2087293827002638525","text":"I can't f*ckn believe this repo is available for FREE.\n\nSomebody built the operator your AI agents have been missing.\n\nLobeHub calls itself your Chief Agent Operator, and it just hit 81,500 stars.\n\n> Hires, schedules, and reports on your AI team 24/7\n> Works with 10,000+ skills"},{"id":"2087556720432431321","au":"ataiiam","t":"2026-08-12T15:08:01.000Z","url":"https://x.com/ataiiam/status/2087556720432431321","text":"Claude Managed Agents  AG-UI\n\n\n@AnthropicAI\n just shipped a full AG-UI integration, so you can bring your Managed Agent to any AG-UI frontend with:\n\n- Generative UI\n- Streaming\n- Tool calls\n- Stateful sessions\n\nIncludes React & React Native, Next.js, Angular as well as Slack,"},{"id":"2087458938329653312","au":"anujcodes_21","t":"2026-08-12T08:39:28.000Z","url":"https://x.com/anujcodes_21/status/2087458938329653312","text":"Every AI conversation starts from scratch. That's not memory. That's amnesia.\n\nThink about it.\n\nYour AI agent talks to a user. It helps them. The session ends.\n\nThe next day, the same user returns. The agent has no idea who they are, what they discussed, or what was resolved."},{"id":"2087486754186248553","au":"imsalariasahil","t":"2026-08-12T10:30:00.000Z","url":"https://x.com/imsalariasahil/status/2087486754186248553","text":"Forget expensive AI courses.  \n\nAnthropic released a free 27-minute Claude prompting workshop, led by the people who built the model.  \n\nNo sign-up. No catch. \n\nSome paid courses don't deliver this much value in hours.  \n\nWatch it."},{"id":"2087567239423676519","au":"GavinSBaker","t":"2026-08-12T15:49:49.000Z","url":"https://x.com/GavinSBaker/status/2087567239423676519","text":"Grok 4.6 is roughly the same performance as Fable 5 Max at an 85% discount. 80% cheaper for input tokens and 88% cheaper for output tokens.\n\nPareto dominant.\n\nGrok 4.7 will be significantly better as is a much larger model with the Cursor and SpaceX data included in pretraining."},{"id":"2087511111767589144","au":"trending_repos","t":"2026-08-12T12:06:47.000Z","url":"https://x.com/trending_repos/status/2087511111767589144","text":"Trending repository of the day \n\nagency-agents\n\nA complete AI agency at your fingertips - From frontend wizards to Reddit community ninjas, from whimsy injectors to reality checkers. Each agent is a specialized e...\n\nLast 24h: 1,969 \nTotal: 144,223 "},{"id":"2087433994480816494","au":"Ronycoder","t":"2026-08-12T07:00:21.000Z","url":"https://x.com/Ronycoder/status/2087433994480816494","text":"Malcolm Gladwell literally gave a 1-hour masterclass on why some people succeed and others don't and it will completely change how you think about talent, effort, and success."},{"id":"2087547168764862495","au":"petergyang","t":"2026-08-12T14:30:04.000Z","url":"https://x.com/petergyang/status/2087547168764862495","text":"I believe the way we use computers will soon change forever.\n\nWe’re moving from doing work manually with a keyboard, mouse, and laptop to directing agents in the cloud using our voices.\n\nIn my new essay, I cover why:\n\n1. Voice is becoming the orchestration layer\n2. Personal"},{"id":"2087362958024417370","au":"Manixh02","t":"2026-08-12T02:18:05.000Z","url":"https://x.com/Manixh02/status/2087362958024417370","text":"Found an open source library of motion effects with 144 options now available.\n\n- CSS React and AI prompt versions included\n- Copy and drop straight into your project\n- Fully free and open source\n\nWorth checking if you need clean animations without the usual setup.\n\nlink;"},{"id":"2087560756309242365","au":"alex_prompter","t":"2026-08-12T15:24:03.000Z","url":"https://x.com/alex_prompter/status/2087560756309242365","text":"Deleting one habit from your AI agent cuts roughly 20% of every response with zero information loss.\n\nThe habit is the trailing summary. Your agent finishes a task, then tells you what it just did. You already have the output sitting right above the recap. Reading it twice adds"},{"id":"2087565882079711599","au":"unclebobmartin","t":"2026-08-12T15:44:26.000Z","url":"https://x.com/unclebobmartin/status/2087565882079711599","text":"If you go to the squad branch of \nhttp://\nGitHub.com/unclebob/swarm\nob/swarm-forge\n… you’ll see what I’ve been spending a lot of time on. \n\nIt’s still in progress, but early results are promising."},{"id":"2087353969605853357","au":"DataChaz","t":"2026-08-12T01:42:22.000Z","url":"https://x.com/DataChaz/status/2087353969605853357","text":"HOLY MOLY\n\n\n@Unsloth\n just dropped their desktop app, and it's the first one designed to let you both run and train models locally \n\nCheck out these specs!\n? Open-source. Runs on Mac, Windows and Linux\n? Supports MLX, diffusion image/video, audio, GGUF\n? Connect Claude Code"},{"id":"2087474422902870513","au":"mikenevermiss","t":"2026-08-12T09:41:00.000Z","url":"https://x.com/mikenevermiss/status/2087474422902870513","text":""},{"id":"2087456734105231761","au":"0xnoonez","t":"2026-08-12T08:30:43.000Z","url":"https://x.com/0xnoonez/status/2087456734105231761","text":"this is f*cking gold\n\nmost people give their agents one giant memory store and call it \"memory\"\n\nthat's not how reliable agents should work\n\nmemory actually splits into four different systems:\n\nWorking ? Episodic ? Semantic ? Procedural\n\nworking memory holds what matters right"},{"id":"2087447507995668929","au":"vikingmute","t":"2026-08-12T07:54:03.000Z","url":"https://x.com/vikingmute/status/2087447507995668929","text":"???????????? Beautiful UI ??????\nhttps://\nbeautifului.dev\n\n???????? vercel ? ai-elements?????????????????? agent ????????????????????????"},{"id":"2087547051718635822","au":"EvanLuthra","t":"2026-08-12T14:29:36.000Z","url":"https://x.com/EvanLuthra/status/2087547051718635822","text":"Instead of watching netflix tonight, watch this billionaire explain how the entire economy works in 42 mins.\n\nWorth more than $200k MBA Program:"},{"id":"2087576557229593033","au":"calcsam","t":"2026-08-12T16:26:51.000Z","url":"https://x.com/calcsam/status/2087576557229593033","text":"Today we're excited to launch dynamic workflows!\n\nDefine a workflow as JSON, and Mastra will validate, register, and run it (like any other workflow).\n\nNow agents can build workflows on-the-fly:"},{"id":"2087257936779481558","au":"0xkkai","t":"2026-08-11T19:20:46.000Z","url":"https://x.com/0xkkai/status/2087257936779481558","text":"IAN SINNOTT SHIPPED AN OBSIDIAN PLUGIN THAT AUTO-CONNECTS CLAUDE CODE TO YOUR VAULT\n\n334 developers already installed it. most people building second brains with claude have no idea it exists\n\nit's obsidian-claude-code-mcp. an obsidian plugin that runs its own MCP server inside"}]}